    "result_text": "All 122 tests pass, including the cp13 test and the full chain of prior checkpoint rules with no regressions.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the per-day owner-creation cap: a `POST /api/owners` request is rejected with **400** once 20 owners already share today's registration date.\n\nChanges, following the OfficeFloor function-injection conventions in `AGENTS.md`:\n\n- **`RejectOverDailyCap.java`** (new function) \u2014 counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()` and throws `BadRequestException` when the count is \u2265 20 (excluding the in-flight owner by id). Newly built owners default `registrationDate` to today in `BuildOwner`, so each accepted create counts toward the cap.\n- **`BadRequestException.java`** (new checked escalation) + **`BadRequestExceptionHandler.java`** \u2014 responds `400` with an empty body, mirroring the existing `ConflictException`/`NotFoundException` pattern.\n- **`...BadRequestException.yml`** (new escalation mapping).\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `rejectOverDailyCap` step (under `govern: [ transaction ]`) into the pipeline after the duplicate-email check and before `save`.\n\nThe 400 mapping is distinct from the existing 409 conflict rules (duplicate telephone/email), matching the spec's requirement of a 400 for a well-formed request that exceeds the daily quota.",
